@ 30.2 - Proto-Potou-Akanic-Bantu to Proto-Potou-Akanic
# citation: Pogostick Man, from Stewart, John M. (2002), “The potential of proto-Potou-Akanic-Bantu as a pilot Proto-Niger-Congo, and the reconstructions updated”. JALL 23:197 – 224
	C > J:[+nas] / #(C)V:[+nas]_
	ɰɰ̃ > l l̃ / #(C)V_
	C > J / #(C)V_
	ɪ(Cɪ) > e(Ci) / t_; “vowel nasalizations are retained either way on each”
	ɟ ʄ j c ɠʷ > c ɟ ʄ t ɠ̥p
	(N)V₁:[+mid +nas](l̃) > CV:[-nas]n
	V:[+nas](ʋ̃,l̃) > V:[-nas](m,n) / #J:[+voice]_